## /etc/config/nssqos
##
## Disabled and emptied of rules deliberately. nssqos is DSCP classification —
## it decides which of the firmware's classes a flow lands in. You said you do
## not want traffic differentiation, only low bufferbloat, and those are
## different jobs: the shaping that controls bufferbloat is sqm's, below.
##
## Running both means two things touching the same queues for no benefit.
## Re-add rules here only if you later want a latency-sensitive class to jump
## the shaped queue.

config global 'global'
	option enabled '0'
